# BZFlag ARM64 Renderer Modernization

This repository carries the Pesky_UK modernization of BZFlag 2.4
for ARM64 Linux (Adreno X1-85, Mesa 26, OpenGL 4.6 compatibility profile).
Upstream BZFlag 2.4 rendered everything through immediate-mode OpenGL
(glBegin/glEnd) and display lists. This fork replaces that draw path with
batched vertex-array rendering, per-pixel GLSL lighting, and shadow mapping —
with no new external libraries — while keeping the compatibility profile so
the rest of the engine remains untouched.

Results (measured in-game on the target machine, ARM64 laptop):

    Before:  15-20 fps, ~15 ms frame lag, 240 glBegin sites, 46 display lists
    After:   120+ fps, 1-2 ms frame lag, 15 glBegin sites (all inside
             display lists, by design), zero display-list tank geometry

A full development log (every change, bug, and measurement) is kept in
`HISTORY.md` at the repository root. The summary below follows that log.

## Platform work

- Migrated the platform layer from SDL 1.2 to SDL 2 (2.32): SDL2Display,
  SDL2Visual, CMake/autotools find_package(SDL2).
- Native ARM64 build (CMakeLists.txt added; CI builds the .deb on
  ubuntu-24.04-arm via GitHub Actions).
- Packaged as `bzflag` .deb (arm64), installed under /usr/local with desktop
  entry and hicolor icons.

## Tier 1 - visual quality (no new libs)

- MSAA (multisample BZDB default 4) via SDL visual attributes; MSAA FBO
  renderbuffer fixed to GL_RGBA.
- Anisotropic texture filtering (default 8, clamped to GL_MAX_TEXTURE_MAX_
  ANISOTROPY), including fonts; maxTextureSize 4096.
- Specular lighting tuned (GL_SPECULAR 0.5*color, tank material
  specular/shininess raised), softer night/day ambient, EXP2 fog with
  sky-tinted color.
- Textures regenerated: 512x512 seamless fbm roof, 512x512 moon.

## Tier 2 - tank rendering

- Stage A: tank geometry off ~450 display lists onto VBOs. A capture layer
  in TankGeometryMgr records builder output into interleaved
  position/normal/uv batches (8 floats per vertex, GL_STATIC_DRAW); triangle
  fans are re-tessellated to triangle soup; per-run shade model recorded and
  restored at draw time.
- Stage B: TankLightingShader - GLSL 1.20 per-pixel Blinn-Phong for tanks,
  reading built-in gl_LightSource/gl_FrontMaterial/gl_Fog so fixed-function
  state needs no mirroring; falls back to fixed pipeline if compile fails.
- Stage C: sun shadow mapping - depth-only FBO (ShadowMapFBO) + per-frame
  sun-space depth pass (ShadowMapper), 4-tap PCF with normal-offset bias in
  the tank shader; BZDB shadowMapSize (default 2048). Falls back to the
  legacy stippled ground shadows when unavailable.

## Tier 3 - de-immediate-mode (GLBatch)

- New GLBatch utility (src/ogl/GLBatch.cxx, include/GLBatch.h): drop-in
  glBegin/glEnd replacement. Accumulates vertices with GL current-value
  semantics and flushes via glDrawArrays; GL_TRIANGLE_FAN drawn natively,
  GL_LINE_LOOP expanded to strip + closing segment; client-array enable bits
  snapshot/restored per flush; current color/normal/texcoord restored to
  match glEnd semantics.
- 97 immediate-mode blocks across 23 files converted in user-verified
  stages (HUD cluster, world/FX cluster, leftovers: radar, walls, mesh,
  flags, tanks, shots, weather lines, debug views). The 15 remaining
  glBegin blocks live inside glNewList/glEndList display lists (fonts, sky,
  celestial bodies, rain) and cannot be captured by glDrawArrays - they are
  intentional.
- Client-array state handling was rebuilt around an explicit
  enable-bit snapshot (glPushClientAttrib removed for performance after
  profiling showed it pure overhead at dozens of flushes per frame).

## Performance work

- GLBatch flush path: native fan draws (no per-frame heap re-tessellation),
  attrib restores trimmed, env lookups cached.
- SceneRenderer setGamma(): full celestial recompute per slider tick
  replaced with cached-base rescaling.
- Server list ping retry budget fixed (retryCount now resets per refresh).
- Measured with the built-in FPS HUD (key T) against the same map/time:
  657 (pre-Tier-3) vs 667-671 (post), and ~30 -> 120+ fps against the
  original pre-Tier-2 build.

## Notable bugs found and fixed (highlights; full list in HISTORY.md)

- Stale static library after src/ogl edits (libtool convenience-archive
  flattening) silently shipping old GLBatch code - rebuild chain:
  ogl -> rm geometry .la/.a -> geometry -> relink, then strings-verify.
- Client-array enable bits left dirty by GLBatch flushes -> untextured
  tanks / white radar blocks; fixed with the begin()/end() snapshot.
- SceneNode.h macro #undef leaking across translation units -> all batched
  colors lost (the "white radar block"); fixed with pragma push/pop_macro.
- Flat-shaded sky from an unrestored glShadeModel in the VBO tank path.
- A central macro-redirect approach for de-immediate-mode was attempted,
  live-tested, and rolled back in favor of hand-edited conversions after
  color-state regressions.
- 2026-09-24 quorum review (3 independent reviewers) + recheck: per-vertex
  color array enable, texcoord-per-vertex staging, buffer-id wrappers
  (bzGenBuffers/bzDeleteBuffers), fan-run draw-mode tagging, and several
  raw-GL-inside-batch sites corrected; tree re-verified clean.

## Client feature: online player list in the server menu (2026-09-26)

- New `ServerQueryPlayers` (src/bzflag): asks the selected game server
  directly for its player list over the standard BZFS handshake — TCP
  connect, BZFLAG connect header, `MsgQueryPlayers` ('qp') request; the
  server answers with a count header plus one `MsgAddPlayer` ('ap') per
  online player. Callsign and team are kept, everything else discarded.
  No third-party service, no list-server change, server code untouched.
- ServerMenu shows the result as an "Online:" line in the left column
  below the team counts (same font as the readouts), team-colored
  callsigns, wrapping to a second line only when the first would run
  off the screen edge.
- Robustness: non-blocking connect polled to completion before the
  header is sent (fixed a send-before-connected race that broke every
  non-loopback server), partial TCP packets wait for more bytes instead
  of aborting, failed/timeout queries auto-retry (2 s throttle, 8 s
  timeout) with no selection change needed.
- Verified protocol-level against a live local bzfs (empty server and
  client-joined server) and signed off in-game by the user on real
  servers (debs 2.4.31-28 .. -32).

## Verification

Every stage was built (make + make check), packaged (deb with icons and
desktop entry verified via dpkg -L), installed, and live-tested in-game with
a scripted harness (local bzfs on port 5154, solo bot, ydotool input, FPS
HUD) before sign-off. The user visually verified each tier and stage.

## Repository

- Upstream: https://github.com/BZFlag-Dev/bzflag (branch 2.4)
- This fork: https://github.com/PC-Support-Services/bzflag (branch 2.4)
- License: unchanged from upstream (LGPL or MPL, see COPYING).

## Building (short version)

    ./autogen.sh && ./configure && make -j4 && make check

or use CMake. The GitHub Actions workflow (.github/workflows/build-deb.yml)
builds the arm64 .deb on every push to 2.4 and attaches it to releases on
tag push (v*).
